Type `make` to generate the CPU executable `runfasteig_cpu`.
With `USE_CUDA=1`, `runfasteig_gpu` is also built.
CPU/GPU executable behavior:
- Use the same input deck for CPU and GPU runs.
- Keep `solver Lanczos` in the input deck.
- Run `./runfasteig_cpu inputfile` to use the CPU Lanczos backend.
- Run `./runfasteig_gpu inputfile` to use the CUDA Lanczos backend.
- The CUDA backend currently supports stored MatrixMarket/CSR Lanczos problems.
  Generalized problems (`bmatrix`) and matrix-free Lanczos should be run with
  `runfasteig_cpu` for now. CUDA `which SAI` requires NVIDIA cuDSS.
macOS quick start (local build)
1) Install Eigen headers (Homebrew):
   `brew install eigen`
2) (Recommended) Enable OpenMP:
   `brew install libomp`
2) Build the library and the example:
   - From repo root (examples will build the library automatically):
     `make -C examples MAKEINC=../make.inc.mac`
3) Run:
   `./runfasteig_cpu SiO.input`
Perlmutter GPU quick start:
  `make USE_CUDA=1`
  `make -C examples USE_CUDA=1`
  `./runfasteig_gpu SiO.input`
CUDA `which SAI` requires NVIDIA cuDSS. If no cuDSS module is available, install
cuDSS into the checkout from the repo root:
  `tools/install_cudss.sh`
  `make -C examples USE_CUDA=1`
If pip download is unavailable, download the Linux cuDSS archive from NVIDIA and
run:
  `tools/install_cudss.sh --tarball /path/to/cudss-linux-*.tar.*`
The default makefile checks for the checkout-local install automatically. On
Perlmutter, a shared project-space install such as
`/global/cfs/cdirs/m1027/Dong/cudss` is also auto-detected when the checkout is
under `/global/cfs/cdirs/m1027/Dong/`. For any other custom cuDSS location,
source the generated `cudss-env.sh` or pass `CUDSS_PATH` and `CUDSS_LIBDIR`
explicitly.
If Eigen is installed somewhere else, override `EIGEN`:
  `make -C examples MAKEINC=../make.inc.mac EIGEN=/path/to/eigen3`
On Linux/UNIX, run the executable by typing
./runfasteig_cpu
for example
./runfasteig_cpu SiO.input
On windows, run the executable by using a batch script to set OpenMP environment properly.
runfasteig.bat SiO.input
runs on a single thread unless the environmental variable FASTEIG_THREADS is larger than 1. This can be done by
set FASTEIG_THREADS=4

